#: ../../source/docs/sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop.rst:5
#: dfbced6bad6b45c8a054bbb5d0c2486e
msgid "SITL Simulator (Software in the Loop)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop.rst:9
#: d8cf281835284082b49460c0204e8fd5
msgid "The SITL (software in the loop) simulator allows you to run Plane, Copter or Rover without any hardware. It is a build of the autopilot code using an ordinary C++ compiler, giving you a native executable that allows you to test the behaviour of the code without hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop.rst:14
#: bcef4f2778174c36b777ade3727fef57
msgid "This article provides an overview of SITL's benefits and architecture."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop.rst:17
#: f1b21f4cb6104c6ebc0ba406bc1424b0
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop.rst:19
#: 6787111bef7f45ba9f8cb6f2665c08cc
msgid "SITL allows you to run ArduPilot on your PC directly, without any special hardware. It takes advantage of the fact that ArduPilot is a portable autopilot that can run on a very wide variety of platforms. Your PC is just another platform that ArduPilot can be built and run on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop.rst:24
#: 8cfd29d650bc40ea9e86c0f8354fc4d2
msgid "When running in SITL the sensor data comes from a flight dynamics model in a flight simulator. ArduPilot has a wide range of vehicle simulators built in, and can interface to several external simulators. This allows ArduPilot to be tested on a very wide variety of vehicle types. For example, SITL can simulate:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop.rst:30
#: 3f6b6efb95ef49648e2e016b36ca54a7
msgid "multi-rotor aircraft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop.rst:31
#: cdce7b6cc0964e7895d2ad35820d0266
msgid "fixed wing aircraft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop.rst:32
#: fa69ee96f88b4ab3bc8b64f4cd395706
msgid "ground vehicles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop.rst:33
#: c324ed3ae188485bbd348ed25cfb6197
msgid "underwater vehicles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop.rst:34
#: d3ee9800bc2a44608aca63eef9509523
msgid "camera gimbals"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop.rst:35
#: 1c3d4861417d41489489e010b712be1b
msgid "antenna trackers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop.rst:36
#: c01585b9b2034888ada3aae51a8ad419
msgid "a wide variety of optional sensors, such as Lidars and optical flow sensors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop.rst:39
#: 310bcf1141234c938343dd313787f7d3
msgid "Adding new simulated vehicle types or sensor types is straightforward."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop.rst:41
#: d2ca9d7fb3f04833ac3b57109f084205
msgid "A big advantage of ArduPilot on SITL is it gives you access to the full range of development tools available to desktop C++ development, such as interactive debuggers, static analyzers and dynamic analysis tools. This makes developing and testing new features in ArduPilot much simpler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop.rst:47
#: d2f34f94b65f4447bf477ecb1296dc17
msgid "Running SITL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop.rst:49
#: 96ae6c6952264e2383b88291f20e9765
msgid "The ArduPilot SITL environment has been developed to run natively on both Linux and Windows. For setup instructions see :ref:`Setting Up SITL <SITL-setup-landingpage>` for more information. Using SITL is explained in :ref:`Using SITL <using-sitl-for-ardupilot-testing>`. For examples of starting and using SITL for a particular vehicle see :ref:`sitl-examples`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop.rst:53
#: 1ce2054348524201af37b7cc0e00a7da
msgid "Mission Planner (Windows) also provides a simple means of running SITL for the master branch and stable branches of vehicles. See :ref:`planner:mission-planner-simulation`."
msgstr ""

